{"term":"imply","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:bec0070912320a226d","definition":"To have as a necessary consequence; to lead to (something) as a consequence.","example":"Correlation does not imply causation","pos":"verb","synonyms":["entail","implicate","import"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["impliable","implier","misimply"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imply#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a1801b8dd202ff6922","definition":"To suggest by logical inference.","example":"When I state that your dog is brown, I am not implying that all dogs are brown.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["impliable","implier","misimply"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imply#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:86bdc9b9fe634ebd43","definition":"To hint; to insinuate; to suggest tacitly and avoid a direct statement.","example":"What do you mean \"we need to be more careful with hygiene\"? Are you implying that I don't wash my hands?","pos":"verb","synonyms":["allude","hint","infer","insinuate","suggest","advert","allude","hint","imply","indicate","inkle","insinuate","intimate","moot","refer","signify","suggest"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["impliable","implier","misimply"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/imply#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b53f87d07634201a7d","definition":"To enfold, entangle.","example":"And in his bosome secretly there lay / An hatefull Snake, the which his taile vptyes / In many folds, and mortall sting implyes.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["enve